 description: >-
-  A translation-invariant CSS qLDPC family built from two sparse binary
-  polynomials on a finite two-dimensional torus. Each polynomial becomes a
-  cyclic-shift matrix; placing the two matrices in H_X=[A|B] and the swapped
-  transposes in H_Z=[B^T|A^T] makes commutation follow from the abelian
-  polynomial algebra. Representative finite blocks trade planar
-  nearest-neighbor layout for a second coupling layer and encode many logical
-  qubits at moderate distance.
+  A CSS code family built by repeating a few parity-check moves on a grid whose
+  opposite edges are identified. Each polynomial term says how far to move on
+  that wrapped grid; the same moves become sparse matrix rows. A swapped,
+  reversed copy supplies the partner checks, while a global rank defect can
+  leave several logical qubits. The two matrix blocks are algebraic coordinate
+  blocks, not by themselves a hardware layout.
 claim_gaps:
   - {property: d, target: wanted:fast-distance}
